<title>UK: Orange up on overseas expansion report.</title>
<headline>Orange up on overseas expansion report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Orange Plc rose to their highest values since early July on a press report that Hutchison Whampoa, a major stakeholder, was to fund an overseas expansion of the UK mobile telephone group, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1017 GMT, the shares were up 2-1/2p at 212-1/2.  </p>
<p>The Financial Times said on Saturday that Hutchison's backing would reassure investors concerned that overseas investment could set back the group's progress in Britain.</p>
<p>Dealers said there was general optimism about Orange's prospects.</p>
<p>&quot;People are looking for good subscriber numbers out of the telecoms group,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
